From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Frida Hou <Frida-a@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:27:11 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [GDN] VLLM_GDN_SPEC_STATE=recover: one state page per request
 in spec decode

Opt-in (env VLLM_GDN_SPEC_STATE=recover, default "per_token" = unchanged)
integration of the records verify + commit for Qwen GDN layers:

- Page layout: gated_delta_net_state_shape/_dtype append the record rings
  (u fp32 [HV, R, V], k act-dtype [H, R, K], g fp32 [HV, R], R = num_spec + 2)
  when enabled; all GDN model classes pass num_spec to the dtype calculator so
  config-time and layer page sizes agree. Qwen GDN layers report
  num_speculative_blocks = 0: one Mamba page per request instead of
  1 + num_speculative_tokens.
- Verify: _forward_core's spec branch calls gdn_recover_verify on q/k/v views
  of the conv output (no rearrange copy) and writes spec-only outputs in
  place; the fused CUDA MTP path is disabled in this mode (the gated RMSNorm
  runs as the separate existing op).
- Commit: GDNRecoverSpecMetadata (a RecoverSSMMetadata) carries the spec
  rows' slots and batch rows; MambaHybridModelState's RecoverSSMState hook
  folds the accepted records for every layer of the group in one launch from
  postprocess_state, right after num_accepted is scattered.
  update_block_table re-targets the commit to each group's layers/slots.
- Guards: fp32 SSM state, mamba_cache_mode "none" (prefix caching / align
  mode not supported yet), CUDA, PP = 1.

Tests: builder metadata (CPU) and a model-path test running _forward_core +
builder for several steps in both modes (bit-identical outputs, conv and
accepted states).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
